    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0388" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/10–2844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4704</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-02">November 2,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State encloses for submission to the European Advisory
                    Commission a U.S. draft paper on “Allied Control Machinery in Germany.” This
                    paper is a redraft of the paper on “Principles of Allied Military Government in
                    Germany,” prepared by the U.S. Advisers, European Advisory Commission.<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d187-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Department of State has approved this redraft. The Joint Chiefs of Staff have
                    given their approval in the manner indicated in the letter from Admiral Leahy to
                    the Secretary of State under date of October 28, 1944. A copy of this
                    communication is also enclosed.</p>






                <xi:include href="d187-a1.xml" xpointer="d187-a1"/>
